  "question": {
    "text": "If in a triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;units, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>cos</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and radius of circumcircle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> units, then the area (in sq. units) of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is:",
    "image": null
